A Python function checks a six-character date of birth typed as DDMMYY. It returns "length", "format", "range" or "ok":

```python
def check(text):
    if len(text) != 6:
        return "length"
    if not text.isdigit():
        return "format"
    if int(text[:2]) > 31:
        return "range"
    return "ok"
```

The function `isdigit()` is true only if every character is a digit. The program is run with four values; the letter in the third value is a capital O, not a zero.
